/**
 * Authenticated user self-service: profile editing, MFA management, password change, and session revocation.
 *
 * <p>This bounded context exposes a self-service portal for authenticated end-users to manage
 * their own identity data. It is distinct from the User context (which handles login and
 * registration) in that it operates on an already-authenticated principal rather than on
 * unauthenticated credentials. All operations are gated by a valid bearer token and scoped
 * to the currently authenticated user's data.
 *
 * <p><b>Key domain types:</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code OidcProfile} — aggregate root representing the user's editable profile. Carries
 *       display name, email address (verified/unverified), preferred language, avatar URL, and
 *       any tenant-defined custom profile attributes. Updated via the self-service form and
 *       persisted through {@code ProfileGateway}.</li>
 *   <li>{@code OidcProfileData} — read projection of profile data formatted for the userinfo
 *       endpoint response, following the OIDC standard claim set (name, email, picture, locale,
 *       sub) and any registered custom claims.</li>
 *   <li>{@code MfaSetup} — value object returned by the MFA-enrollment panel initialization.
 *       Carries the TOTP QR-code URL and base32 secret from the MFA context, along with the
 *       current MFA enrollment status (enabled / disabled) for the profile UI to render.</li>
 *   <li>{@code ActiveSession} — value object representing a currently active authorization
 *       session for the user. Carries the session identifier, originating client name, creation
 *       timestamp, last-activity timestamp, and the IP address / user-agent of the session,
 *       enabling the user to identify and revoke sessions from unrecognized devices.</li>
 *   <li>{@code ProfileGateway} — port for reading and persisting the user's {@code OidcProfile}.
 *       Implementations read from and write to the user-profile table in the persistence layer.</li>
 *   <li>{@code MfaGateway} — port for enabling and disabling TOTP MFA on the user's account,
 *       bridging the Profile context to the MFA context without direct coupling.</li>
 *   <li>{@code PasswordGateway} — port for changing the user's password from the self-service
 *       portal, equivalent in contract to the User context's {@code ChangePasswordGateway} but
 *       scoped to the authenticated-user use case (no old-password re-verification required when
 *       invoked after fresh authentication).</li>
 *   <li>{@code SessionsGateway} — port for listing the user's active sessions and for revoking
 *       a specific session by identifier, enabling the session-management panel in the portal.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Key application services:</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code ProfileService} — facade aggregating all self-service operations:
 *       {@code getProfile}, {@code saveProfile} (name, email, avatar updates),
 *       {@code enableMfa} / {@code disableMfa} (delegates to the MFA context),
 *       {@code changePassword} (via {@code PasswordGateway}),
 *       {@code listSessions} (returns all {@code ActiveSession} records for the user),
 *       and {@code revokeSession} (invalidates a specific session by ID).</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Infrastructure drivers and adapters:</b>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>{@code ProfileHtmlController} — HTML driver rendering the multi-panel self-service portal.
 *       Each panel is a separate Qute template rendered via the Theme context decorator.</li>
 *   <li>{@code ProfileViewPanel} / {@code ProfileEditPanel} — display and edit panels for profile data.</li>
 *   <li>{@code ChangePasswordPanel} — panel handling old-password verification and new-password
 *       submission with client-side strength feedback.</li>
 *   <li>{@code MfaPanel} — panel for MFA enable/disable and QR code enrollment display.</li>
 *   <li>{@code SessionsPanel} — panel listing active sessions with per-session revocation buttons.</li>
 *   <li>{@code HtmlEscape} — utility used within panel templates to prevent XSS in rendered
 *       user-controlled data such as display names and email addresses.</li>
 *   <li>{@code ProfileMeController} — REST driver implementing GET /userinfo and
 *       PATCH /me for programmatic profile updates, used by mobile or SPA clients.</li>
 *   <li>{@code ProfileAdapter} / {@code MfaAdapter} / {@code PasswordAdapter} / {@code SessionsAdapter}
 *       — driven SQL adapters for each gateway contract.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <p><b>Internal structure:</b>
 * <pre>
 * profile/
 * ├── domain/
 * │   ├── OidcProfile.java / OidcProfileData.java / MfaSetup.java / ActiveSession.java
 * │   └── gateway/   — ProfileGateway, MfaGateway, PasswordGateway, SessionsGateway
 * ├── application/
 * │   └── ProfileService.java           — self-service facade
 * └── infrastructure/
 *     ├── driven/    — ProfileAdapter, MfaAdapter, PasswordAdapter, SessionsAdapter
 *     └── driver/
 *         ├── html/  — ProfileHtmlController + panels (View, Edit, ChangePassword, Mfa, Sessions)
 *         └── rest/  — ProfileMeController
 * </pre>
 *
 * <p><b>Dependencies:</b> Requires a valid bearer token (Authentication context). Delegates MFA
 * operations to the MFA context. Depends on Session context for session listing and revocation.
 * Shares the user-profile persistence schema with the User context.
 *
 * <p><b>Stability:</b> stable for core operations; the panel system is the most likely evolution
 * point as new self-service capabilities (passkey management, email change verification flow) are
 * added.
 */
package net.civeira.phylax.features.oauth.profile;
